6)What are some Terraform best practices you follow in production environments?
In production, I follow a modular Terraform structure with separate environments and remote state storage with locking using S3 + DynamoDB.
I use version pinning, variables, and secret managers to avoid hardcoding.
We enforce GitOps flow, where Terraform runs via CI/CD with plan → approval → apply steps. 
All resources are tagged properly, and RBAC policies ensure only authorized users apply changes to Prod. 
These practices help with stability, security, and consistency of infrastructure deployments.
